data
runs
runs/
posts/template
# posts/*/figures are regenerated by the notebook and are git-ignored (the repo
# tracks code + prose, not artifacts). The one committed copy lives under
# site/images/posts/<slug>/ (sync_posts.py copies the article-referenced figures
# there for the deployed site, which Vercel cannot regenerate). CI copies those
# back into figures/ for a prose-only PDF build so the notebook need not re-run.
#
# Hand-authored images (diagrams, photos, anything the notebook does NOT
# generate) do not belong here — nothing would recreate them on a fresh
# checkout. They go in the tracked posts/*/assets/ instead.
posts/*/figures
posts/*/out
posts/*/out/
posts/*/out/*
# Rendered post PDFs and LaTeX build artifacts
posts/*/*.pdf
posts/*/*.aux
posts/*/*.log
posts/*/*.fls
posts/*/*.fdb_latexmk
posts/*/*.out
posts/*/*.synctex.gz
output
output/
outputs
outputs/
# Don't ignore the Susy vendor stylesheets, whose source dir is literally named "output/"
!site/_sass/vendor/susy/susy/output/
!site/_sass/vendor/susy/susy/output/**
tmp.*
**/.lake
posts/**/data
.vercel
CLAUDE.md
.claude
# ── Unpublished site sections ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC, and Vercel builds the site from what is committed here.
# So "don't publish it yet" means "don't commit it yet" — front matter alone
# (published: false) would still put the text on GitHub for anyone to read.
#
# These are name patterns, not a list of specific files, so that this committed
# file gives away nothing about what is being drafted. Anything matching builds
# on a local `jekyll serve` and never leaves this machine:
#
#   *.draft.*          a draft page or collection entry (permalink and date come
#                      from front matter, so the filename can be anything)
#   _data/*_local.yml  a draft section's content, or an overlay of draft entries
#                      appended to an existing section (see _pages/software.html)
#   images/drafts/     any image those drafts use
#
# See DEVELOPMENT.md, "Unpublished sections", for the three staging patterns and
# how to publish one. To see what is currently held back:
#   git status --ignored --short site
site/**/*.draft.*
site/_data/*_local.yml
site/images/drafts/
